{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["<b>לוא</b> — Some say it is from the root of \"אלה,\" and we have not found it without alef. Its meaning: what has come upon me will not come upon you." "<b>עולל</b> — Was done to me. And it belongs to the heavy stem [pu'al] whose verbal noun is not designated, because it does not have kamatz katan, like: כונן אשורי." "<b>הוגה</b> — Like: הרה."], :book :lamentations, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {0 "The reading of the gloss is uncertain; translated hyper-literally."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Lamentations -- Wikisource" "https://he.wikisource.org/wiki/%D7%90%D7%91%D7%9F_%D7%A2%D7%96%D7%A8%D7%90_%D7%A2%D7%9C_%D7%9E%D7%92%D7%99%D7%9C%D7%AA_%D7%90%D7%99%D7%9B%D7%94"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:07:26.673042761Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}